From d7c97dc2bb2a30c9b2d465b782527f523091962b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 08:57:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add a Logs page listing log files from the configured logs
 directory

New /logs route (wired to the nav bar's existing 'Logs' item, previously
a placeholder), using the same data-table search/page-size/pagination
UI as Site Blocks -- no filter dropdown, since there's nothing to
filter by yet.

Rotated log files (Caddy's roll_size/roll_keep/roll_keep_for backups,
named <prefix>-<timestamp>-<reason><ext>, optionally .gz/.zst
compressed) are grouped back under the live log they rolled from, so
each row is one logical log stream rather than one file. A row shows
the live filename, a +N badge when N-1 rotated backups exist alongside
it, and the most recent mtime across the whole group as 'Updated'. A
disabled 'View' button is in place for now, per the request that
viewing a log's contents is a follow-up.

New caddy_manager/logs.py holds the grouping logic (logical_log_name +
list_log_files), kept separate from blocks.py since it scans the logs
directory directly rather than cross-referencing block metadata --
every file in logs_dir is listed, whether or not it was written by a
block this app manages.

Verified: unit checks on logical_log_name covering uncompressed/gzip/
zstd rotated names, a custom rotation reason tag, and a base filename
that itself contains dashes (to rule out false positives); a Flask
test-client check of grouping counts/timestamps and full-page rendering
(badge, search/page-size/pagination present, no filter dropdown,
disabled View button, nav link wired and marked active); confirmed
every other page still renders with the updated nav.html. Full prior
regression suite (logging, rotation, disable toggle) still passes.
pyflakes clean.
